From e56a4dba50302b6d9b6f2227e9ec9645048f2225 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:04:48 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(bore): refuse a bore too wide for its ring, and keep
 it out of Detect holes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Bore ride is a centre dive, one radial sweep and one ring on the
wall. Past 3 x tool diameter + 2 x stock to leave the dive's disc and
the ring's band no longer meet, so a through bore freed a core (the
issue's Ø74.3 bore with a 4 mm tool left a Ø66 disc) and still
generated and verified ok.

- motion: the bore kernel refuses such a hole at its door with the
  hole, cutter, ring radius, core size and limit named;
  max_bore_diameter() states the limit once.
- app: detect_holes on a Bore op keeps only the holes its tool clears
  and names each one left out (DetectedHoles.skipped); all too wide is
  a refusal. MCP detect_holes answers `skipped`; the GUI status line
  says the same.
- Pins: bore_core_tests (refusal numbers, the limit, floor coverage
  law), tests/bore_core.rs (MCP), detect_holes_note_tests (GUI).

Fixes #1556

